hadley wickham wrote:

> R isn't very good at detecting when package dependencies also need to
> be updated, so you probably need to do:
>
> install.packages(c("reshape","plyr"))

I never experienced R wasn't good at detecting this.

On the other hand, if a new version of a package relies
on a new version of another one, it should be stated
using explicit versions in the "Depends:" field.

It is a different thing to depend on a package and
to depend on a specific (sufficiently recent) version
of a package. I notice reshape does not have such
a 'versioned dependency' on plyr, which might cause
the problems.

Best,
Tobias

