Hi Baptiste,

There are three things you need to do if you're adapting an existing geom:

 * make sure the geom object itself has a new name
 * make sure the objname property is unique
 * create the friendly accessor function which looks like
  geom_point <- GeomPoint$build_accessor()

I've also attached a very very very rough draft of a writing your own
chapter that didn't make it into the book - it may (or may not) be
helpful.

Hadley

